# Keeps the build context small - none of this is needed inside the image (configs/ and
# data/ are bind-mounted at runtime per docker-compose.yml, so they don't need to be baked in
# too; the rest is local dev cruft). models/ is NOT excluded - docker-compose.yml doesn't mount
# it as a volume, so the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` is what actually gets model weights into the
# image; excluding it would silently ship an ingestion image with no weights.
.git
.venv*
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
node_modules
data
scratch_test
services/dashboard/node_modules
services/dashboard/dist
